th an invented `SELECT`.\n- A guard it cannot decompose is returned whole. One condition treated as atomic\n  is a weaker claim than a wrong decomposition.\n\nA fabricated answer is worse than an absent one, because an absent one is\nvisibly absent.\n\n## What it is for, then\n\nRecovering a behaviour model from code, comparing it against what somebody said\nthe system should do, and generating human-executable test cases from the part\nthat survives human review. Everything above is in service of the last clause.\n executes against sut code derived code derived", ordinal: 1}, {path: "02-the-shape-of-the-model.md", lifecycle_state: "Quarantine", m_project: "metis", source_episode_id: "ep-lessons-f300da3676163a62", embedding_model: "minishlab/potion-base-8M", name: "The shape of the model", embedding: [-0.16944965720176697, 0.21060873568058014, -0.39939501881599426, -0.14841535687446594, 0.20901800692081451, 0.07980847358703613, 0.06391508877277374, -0.06853197515010834, -0.11270958930253983, -0.0050389827229082584, -0.16958987712860107, 0.05965695530176163, -0.1261565238237381, 0.04701055586338043, 0.017080333083868027, 0.023050785064697266, 0.004483128432184458, 0.08225454390048981, -0.015922369435429573, -0.09469832479953766, 0.025112705305218697, 0.07666154950857162, -0.00039192201802507043, -0.11913037300109863, -0.05448637157678604, 0.07350907474756241, 0.014351890422403812, -0.11338566988706589, -0.0866461843252182, 0.05696222186088562, -0.13149785995483398, 0.04644019156694412, 0.04422849789261818, 0.0707230344414711, 0.09970109164714813, 0.06532213091850281, 0.15962503850460052, -0.08414202928543091, -0.09938860684633255, -0.01342601515352726, -0.02866186760365963, -0.04261210560798645, 0.020940527319908142, 0.004784827586263418, -0.05723286047577858, -0.019420664757490158, 0.029933230951428413, -0.04982573911547661, -0.044442955404520035, 0.02439759112894535, -0.027495678514242172, -0.07276011258363724, -0.034773122519254684, -0.053880754858255386, -0.05464