88469041883945, 0.006169954780489206, 0.012016991153359413, 0.050345901399850845, -0.006898475810885429], id: "lesson:01-what-metis-does-not-do#02", text: "## It never executes anything against the system under test\n\n**X-7a.** M\u00e9tis reads intake sources and writes its own graph. It does not call\nthe API it models, drive the UI it models, or run a query against the database\nit models.\n\nThe distinction that does the work: *a database M\u00e9tis reads to learn structure\nis an intake source; the same database reached to check a test's outcome is the\nsystem under test.* Same server, different act, and only the first is available.\n\nThis is structural rather than remembered. Every `access` mode in\n`connectors/intakes.json` is read-only, `executes_against_sut` is a schema\n`const` of `false`, and the loader refuses a declaration that says otherwise.\nThere is deliberately **no mode meaning \"runs something\"**. Adding one is the\nchange that would have to be argued for.", search_text: "It never executes anything against the system under test ## It never executes anything against the system under test\n\n**X-7a.** Metis reads intake sources and writes its own graph. It does not call\nthe API it models, drive the UI it models, or run a query against the database\nit models.\n\nThe distinction that does the work: *a database Metis reads to learn structure\nis an intake source; the same database reached to check a test's outcome is the\nsystem under test.* Same server, different act, and only the first is available.\n\nThis is structural rather than remembered. Every `access` mode in\n`connectors/intakes.json` is read-only, `executes_against_sut` is a schema\n`const` of `false`, and the loader refuses a declaration that says otherwise.\nThere is deliberately **no mode meaning \"runs something\"**. Adding one is the\nchange that would have to be argued for. executes against sut", ordinal: 2}, {m_project: "metis", source_episode_id: "ep-lessons-f300da3676163a62", 