.00989430584013462, 0.0007167649455368519, 0.030452989041805267, -0.003708210773766041, 0.004044495057314634, 0.014536382630467415, -0.030135666951537132, 0.00036615191493183374, 4.2927935282932594e-05, 0.03341103717684746, 0.0009164807852357626, 0.004879804328083992, 0.022967029362916946, -0.01165918167680502, 0.020940659567713737, -0.01452406495809555, 0.04115242138504982, 0.03527597337961197, 0.038156576454639435, -0.024068091064691544, -0.001929032034240663, -0.06168263778090477, 0.003916971385478973, -0.0030897604301571846, 0.030462946742773056, 0.00037207535933703184, 0.028244348242878914, -0.006853819824755192], ordinal: 5, search_text: "The ontology is closed ## The ontology is closed\n\n65 labels, and `metis_mcp/ontology/labels.py` is the single source: `LABELS`,\n`ALLOWED_RELATIONSHIPS`, and `STAGED_OUT` \u2014 the deliberately-excluded labels,\neach recorded with the trigger that would bring it back. An absence with a\nreason is a decision; an absence without one is an oversight.\n\nThe Cypher schema is **generated** from `labels.py`, so those two cannot drift.\nAdding a label or a relationship is a reviewed change under **D-2**, and **D-1**\nsets the bar: a label needs a named writer *and* a named reader. A label nothing\nwrites is a promise; a label nothing reads is a cost.\n\nHand-written Cypher is the place D-2 cannot generate, so a test scans every\nCypher string in the tree and fails on a label the ontology does not have.\nThat check exists because staging out `Field` left\n`(t)-[:REQUIRES]->(f:Field)` in a query: still valid Cypher, matching nothing,\nreturning an empty list, failing nothing. metis mcp ALLOWED RELATIONSHIPS STAGED OUT"}, {m_project: "metis", source_episode_id: "ep-lessons-f300da3676163a62", embedding_model: "minishlab/potion-base-8M", name: "3 \u00b7 Facts, evidence, and why nothing is approved", embedding: [-0.1673828363418579, 0.19174255430698395, -0.06268741935491562, 0.014025971293449402, 0.2150881588459015, -0.0172946937382221