ode says one thing. The OpenAPI document says another. Neither is trusted\nover the other, and the disagreement is the output:\n\n| | Routes |\n|---|---|\n| Both sources describe | 9 |\n| Contract only | `POST /record/{id}/restore` |\n| Code only | `POST /record/{id}/archive` |\n\nA model extracted from code and used to test that code proves the code does what\nthe code does (**\u00a74.1**). *The code locks after 3 attempts; the criterion says 5*\nis the finding no amount of self-testing produces.", id: "lesson:06-from-a-repository-to-test-cases#04", search_text: "The comparison is the point ## The comparison is the point\n\nThe code says one thing. The OpenAPI document says another. Neither is trusted\nover the other, and the disagreement is the output:\n\n| | Routes |\n|---|---|\n| Both sources describe | 9 |\n| Contract only | `POST /record/{id}/restore` |\n| Code only | `POST /record/{id}/archive` |\n\nA model extracted from code and used to test that code proves the code does what\nthe code does (**\u00a74.1**). *The code locks after 3 attempts; the criterion says 5*\nis the finding no amount of self-testing produces.", ordinal: 4}, {m_project: "metis", source_episode_id: "ep-lessons-f300da3676163a62", embedding_model: "minishlab/potion-base-8M", name: "Why a whole service is re-extracted every time", id: "lesson:06-from-a-repository-to-test-cases#05", embedding: [-0.19762305915355682, 0.1414409577846527, -0.2263205200433731, -0.1444718837738037, 0.12959910929203033, 0.06955800205469131, -0.03192475438117981, -0.15012617409229279, -0.1374673694372177, 0.16849587857723236, -0.1851465106010437, 0.10816095024347305, -0.11685402691364288, -0.048829831182956696, 0.0655917376279831, -0.05028660595417023, -0.04575944319367409, -0.0010297904955223203, 0.009505652822554111, -0.09784325212240219, 0.0027382869739085436, -0.06796848028898239, 0.1694522649049759, -0.026484809815883636, -0.07445397228002548, -0.016048433259129524, 0.05860259756445885, -0.076893649995327, 0.0