50450219959, -0.02255932427942753, 0.05964253470301628, -0.02178039960563183, 0.029758362099528313, 0.008746926672756672, 0.006343631073832512, -0.03717080503702164, -0.03902542591094971, 0.021633150056004524, -0.026074877008795738, 0.03797675669193268, 0.008521050214767456, 0.00745995482429862, -0.009864895604550838, 0.04829695075750351, -0.022181296721100807, -0.03869803622364998, -0.004307241644710302, -0.06562639772891998, 0.02065880410373211, 0.034589558839797974, 0.024529650807380676, -0.10288015007972717, 0.014448733069002628, -0.036870669573545456, 0.0381292887032032, -0.030373767018318176, 0.010595996864140034, -0.018072236329317093, -0.027501819655299187, 0.007579536642879248, -0.01438840664923191, 0.02947075106203556, -0.04776580259203911, -0.0744946226477623, -0.03626678138971329, 0.07306791841983795, -0.01639498583972454, 0.01639079861342907, 0.03436742350459099, -0.03881090506911278, 0.017898576334118843, 0.008843584917485714, 0.03264473378658295, -0.0027175631839782, 0.013199111446738243, 0.019900761544704437, -0.0069594187662005424, 0.06731195002794266, 0.004948964808136225, 0.001028598751872778, 0.006759907118976116, -0.011948357336223125, 0.006639130413532257, -0.04727470129728317, -0.036231424659490585, -0.020355861634016037, -0.017775759100914, -0.028600728139281273, 0.02675021067261696, 0.016255466267466545, -0.000399038806790486], text: "## Two traps, and how they are closed\n\n**A re-run must not resurrect a superseded fact.** Validity is written by\n`ON CREATE SET`, so a routine re-extraction cannot reset `valid_to` to empty. An\ninvalidation that an unrelated re-run can undo is not an invalidation.\n\n**A read that ignores validity answers the wrong question.** It reports what was\n*ever* believed while looking like it reports what is believed *now*, and that\nfailure is indistinguishable from success. Every read over a validity-carrying\nlabel filters on it, and a test asserts that with an exemption list that is\ncurrently empty.", id: "lesson:07-time-what-was-true-and-when#04", search_text: "Two traps, and how they are closed ## Two traps, and how they are closed\n\n**A re-run must not resurrect a superseded fact.** Validity is written by\n`ON CREATE SET`, so a routine re-extraction cannot reset `valid_to` to empty. An\ninvalidation that an unrelated re-run can undo is not an invalidation.\n\n**A read that ignores validity answers the wrong question.** It reports what was\n*ever* believed while looking like it reports what is believed *now*, and that\nfailure is indistinguishable from success. Every read over a validity-carrying\nlabel filters on it, and a test asserts that with an exemption list that is\ncurrently empty. valid to", ordinal: 4}, {m_project: "metis", source_episode_id: "ep-lessons-f300da3676163a62", embedding_model: "minishlab/potion-base-8M", name: "Reading the past", text: "## Reading the past\n\n    default read    \u2192 currently valid\n    as-at read      \u2192 valid_from <= T < valid_to\n\nThe interval is **half-open** on purpose: a fact invalidated at `T` was true up\nto `T` and not at `T`. Closing both ends would make it briefly true and\nsuperseded at once.", id: "lesson:07-time-what-was-true-and-when#05", embedding: [-0.32482317090034485, 0.09576885402202606, -0.3215460479259491, 0.03969106450676918, 0.19104519486427307, 0.20210853219032288, 0.02525091916322708, -0.10081814974546432, -0.04619448632001877, 0.028332427144050598, -0.11719199270009995, -0.028930632397532463, -0.13579654693603516, -0.02294144034385681, 0.00038705056067556143, -0.032111912965774536, -0.04954246059060097, 0.012048322707414627, 0.037158891558647156, -0.1286434382200241, 0.05922083929181099, 0.13082510232925415, 0.03161389008164406, -0.10722432285547256, -0.11355974525213242, 0.08516228944063187, 0.06458365172147751, -0.041072338819503784, -0.08953259885311127, 0.07449167966842651, -0.048966407775878906, 0.06156020238995552, 0.055517666041851044, -0.020338527858257294, 0.10830312967300415, 0.063900